jobs.description:
Do you enjoy hands-on work and staying physically active?

For DHL Supply Chain in Beringe, we are looking for enthusiastic Warehouse Employees Loading & Unloading. In this varied role, you play an important part in the logistics process by ensuring goods are handled safely, efficiently, and on time.

Experience with a forklift or reach truck is a plus, but not required. If you are motivated and willing to learn, we are happy to hear from you. Your attitude and commitment matter more than experience.

What will you do?

As a Warehouse Employee Loading & Unloading, you are responsible for processing incoming and outgoing goods flows. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that trucks are loaded and unloaded on time and that goods are stored in the correct locations within the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading trucks, both manually and with logistics equipment;
- Checking incoming and outgoing goods for accuracy and quantity;
- Moving, sorting, and storing goods within the warehouse;
- Maintaining a safe, clean, and organized working environment;
- Collaborating with colleagues to ensure smooth logistics operations;
- Supporting various warehouse activities.

Please note: this role involves physically demanding work.

Working hours

You will work in a 3-shift system:

- 06:00 – 15:00
- 09:00 – 18:00
- 15:00 – 00:00

During your onboarding period, you will typically start in the 09:00 – 18:00 shift.

You are motivated, flexible, and enjoy active work. You are accurate and feel comfortable in a fast-paced logistics environment.

In addition, you have:

- VMBO level education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- Full-time availability;
- Willingness to work in shifts;
- Good command of the English language;
- Basic knowledge of geography is a plus;
- Living within 50 km of Beringe;
- Experience in logistics is an advantage but not required;
- Willingness to learn how to operate a forklift and/or reach truck, or already certified.

As a Forklift and/or Reach Truck Operator, you are responsible for keeping the warehouse and shipping process running efficiently. Your daily tasks include collecting and moving goods, scanning shipments, checking orders for accuracy, loading and unloading trucks, and maintaining a clean and safe working environment. You are also happy to support other departments whenever needed, because teamwork is at the heart of DSV.

You will work full-time (40 hours per week) in a fixed team at the Moerdijk warehouse and are willing to work in a two-shift schedule.

- Valid Forklift and/or Reach Truck certificate;
- At least 1 year of experience operating a forklift or reach truck;
- Full-time availability (40 hours per week) willing to work a fixed two-shift schedule (06:00 - 15:00, 07:00 - 16:00, 08:00 - 17:00, or 15:00 - 00:00);
- Own transportation and willingness to work in Moerdijk;
- You are at least 18 years old and a VMBO or MBO working thinking level (or equivalent);
- You have a good command of the English language;
- Accurate, safety-conscious, and a team player;

Would you like to contribute to flawless mail delivery and are you looking for a flexible part-time job? Become a mail preparer at our client in Assen! In this role, you will be responsible for ensuring that mail is correctly sorted and prepared for dispatch.

As a mail preparer in Assen, you are responsible for accurately sorting incoming mail. You will check addresses and shipping details and use various mail processing machines to handle the mail efficiently. The job requires precision and good physical condition, as you will be working primarily on your feet. You should also be open to working overtime to assist your colleagues during backlogs or busy periods.

What we ask for:

- No minimum educational requirements;
- Precision and attention to detail;
- Enthusiastic and motivated attitude;
- You speak either Dutch or English;
- Availability for 3 days, between Monday to Thursday.

Are you looking for an active job with variety in your tasks? FedEx in Duiven is looking for logistic employees. Your job is to make sure that all packages will reach their destination in time.

Your hourly salary can be €21,22 including shift allowance.

What are you going to do?
In this dynamic role, you'll ensure the smooth running of the sorting process. Your duties include:

• Sorting and processing incoming packages;

• Efficiently loading packages onto trucks;

• Collaborating with colleagues to meet deadlines.

You'll work the following shifts:

2:30 PM – 11:00 PM

5:30 PM – 1:00 AM

11:00 PM – 7:00 AM

What do we offer?
• Gross hourly wage of €15,16, with allowances up to €21,22 per hour;

• Prospects of permanent employment with FedEx;

• 8% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days;

• Travel allowance of €0,25 per kilometer;

• Pension accrual through Adecco from age 18;

• Access to the Adecco Academy for training and courses;

• A pleasant, safe work environment with dedicated colleagues.

Where will you work?
FedEx is one of the world's largest logistics service providers, shipping millions of packages daily from Duiven to over 200 countries. Working safely, collaborating, and continuously growing are our top priorities. Your efforts are recognized and appreciated.

What do we ask?
• You speak Dutch or English fluently;

• You can apply for a Certificate of Conduct (costs will be reimbursed);

• You have your own transportation;

• You can be deployed flexible.

Are you interested?
Ready to get started? Click the application button and take the next step in your career!

Questions? Send a message or call Sanne at 06 42506892. You can apply for this position until September 27th, 2026.

As an Administrative Customs Coordinator, you play a vital role in ensuring international shipments cross borders smoothly and comply with customs regulations. You will be responsible for processing customs declarations accurately and ensuring all documentation meets legal requirements. No customs experience? No problem. DHL provides comprehensive training and offers a Junior Broker Course, allowing you to build a successful career in the customs and logistics industry.

What You'll Do

- Prepare, process, and monitor customs declarations;
- Review and verify shipment documentation for accuracy and compliance;
- Track and manage the progress of customs files and declarations;
- Communicate with customers, colleagues, and external stakeholders;
- Identify and resolve administrative discrepancies;
- Follow customs procedures and applicable regulations to ensure compliance;

- Strong attention to detail and accuracy;
-  Excellent organizational and administrative skills;
-  Good command of the English language, both written and spoken;
-  Strong communication and problem-solving abilities;
-  Experience in administration, logistics, customer service, or a related field is an advantage, but not required;
-  A proactive attitude and willingness to learn.
